==Central Franconian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|gmw-cfr|kumme||some Ripuarian dialects, including Kölsch}}
* {{alter|gmw-cfr|kun|kunn|konn||Ripuarian; some Moselle Franconian dialects; chiefly dated}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gmw-cfr|goh|kweman}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|gmw-pro|*kweman}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|gem-pro|*kwemaną}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|ine-pro|*gʷémt}}. The form is native in Moselle Franconian, but borrowed from {{der|gmw-cfr|de|-}} in Ripuarian.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gmw-cfr|/ˈkomə/}}

===Verb===
{{head|gmw-cfr|verb|third-person singular present|kennt|or|kött|past tense|kom|past participle|komme|or|jekomme|or|gekomme}}

# to [[come]]

====Usage notes====
* The present conjugation in [[Moselle Franconian]] goes: ''du'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kenns}}, ''hä'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kennt}}, ''dir'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kommt}}.
* The present conjugation in [[Ripuarian]] goes: ''du'' {{m|gmw-cfr|köss}}, ''hä'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kött}}, ''ühr'' {{m|gmw-cfr|kott}}. These forms are vestiges of the old infinitive ''konn, kunn''.

==Danish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|da|gmq-oda|komæ}}, {{m|gmq-oda|kommæ}}, {{m|gmq-oda|kombæ}}, from {{der|da|non|koma}}, from {{der|da|gem-pro|*kwemaną}}, cognate with {{cog|en|come}}, {{cog|de|kommen}}. The Germanic verb goes back to {{der|da|ine-pro|*gʷem-||to step}}, cf. {{cog|la|veniō}}, {{cog|grc|βαίνω}} (whence also {{m|da|base}} and {{m|da|basis}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|da|[ˈkʰʌmə]|[ˈkʰʌmm̩]}}
* {{rhymes|da|ɒmə}}

===Verb===
{{head|da|verb|imperative|kom|present|kommer|past|kom|past participle|kommet|{{g|c}}|kommen|definite or plural|komne}}

# to [[come]]
#: {{ux|da|'''Kom''' med mig|Come with me}}
# to [[get]]
# {{lb|da|intransitive}} To [[appear]], to [[manifest]] itself; [[come]]
#: {{ux|da|Smerten i benet '''kommer''' og går|The pain in his leg '''comes''' and goes.}}
# to [[arrive]]
#: {{ux|da|Han '''kom''' i tid|He came on time}}
# to [[put]]
#: {{ux|da|Han '''kom''' glasur på|He put frosting on}}
# to reach [[orgasm]]; to [[come]]
#: {{ux|da|Han '''kom''' i min hånd|He came in my hand}}

